<section id="the-short-version">
  <h2>
    <span class="section-icon">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="8" y1="6" x2="21" y2="6"/><line x1="8" y1="12" x2="21" y2="12"/><line x1="8" y1="18" x2="21" y2="18"/><circle cx="4" cy="6" r="1"/><circle cx="4" cy="12" r="1"/><circle cx="4" cy="18" r="1"/></svg>
    </span>
    The Short Version
  </h2>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>What we keep:</strong> your conversations, the things you tell Ferni, and your account details.</li>
    <li><strong>Why:</strong> so Ferni can remember you next time. That's the whole point.</li>
    <li><strong>Who processes it:</strong> it's stored on Google Cloud, and a short list of companies help run Ferni. <a href="#data-sharing">Every one is named below.</a></li>
    <li><strong>What we never do:</strong> sell your data, show you ads, or train models on your conversations.</li>
    <li><strong>How to delete it:</strong> in the app, open the menu, choose <strong>Privacy &amp; your data</strong>, then <strong>Delete my account</strong>. What Ferni saved is erased right away.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>One honest gap: deleting your account doesn't erase usage analytics yet. They never include what you said, and they're deleted after 400 days.</p>
</section>

