<section id="ai-and-ml">
  <h2>
    <span class="section-icon">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2c0 .74-.4 1.39-1 1.73V7h1a7 7 0 0 1 7 7h1a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v3a1 1 0 0 1-1 1h-1v1a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-1H2a1 1 0 0 1-1-1v-3a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h1a7 7 0 0 1 7-7h1V5.73c-.6-.34-1-.99-1-1.73a2 2 0 0 1 2-2z"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="14.5" r="1.5"/><circle cx="16.5" cy="14.5" r="1.5"/></svg>
    </span>
    Models and Your Conversations
  </h2>

  <p>Ferni runs on large language models. Here's how that touches your data:</p>

  <h3>How Ferni Thinks</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Our AI specialists (Ferni, Maya, Peter, Alex, Jordan, Nayan) use large language models to understand and respond to you</li>
    <li>Your conversation history enables personalized, continuous coaching</li>
    <li>AI analyzes patterns in your conversations to provide relevant insights</li>
    <li>Ferni doesn't identify you by the sound of your voice, and doesn't make a copy of your voice. Neither is offered today. If we ever offer them, they'll be off until you give your explicit consent, and you'll be able to turn them off</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Training</h3>
  <div class="callout callout--important">
    <strong>We don't train models on your conversations.</strong>
    <p>Not ours, and there's no setting that turns it on. If that ever changes, we'll ask you first and update this policy.</p>
  </div>

  <p>The companies whose models write Ferni's replies don't train on what we send them either. Their terms say so: <a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/data-governance">Google's Vertex AI</a> and the <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/terms">paid Gemini API</a>, <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal/commercial-terms">Anthropic's commercial terms</a>, and <a href="https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/your-data">OpenAI's API</a>. So do <a href="https://livekit.com/legal/terms-of-service">LiveKit's</a>.</p>

  <p>Cartesia, which turns your voice into text and Ferni's words into speech, works differently: <a href="https://cartesia.ai/legal/terms">its terms</a> let it learn from customers' audio and text unless the customer opts out. We've opted Ferni out.</p>

  <h3>Automated Decision-Making</h3>
  <p>Ferni does not make legally or similarly significant decisions about you through purely automated means. Our AI provides coaching suggestions and insights, but you always maintain full control over your decisions and actions.</p>
</section>

<section id="google-user-data">
  <h2>
    <span class="section-icon">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="14" rx="2"/><path d="M3 7l9 6 9-6"/></svg>
    </span>
    Google User Data
  </h2>

  <div class="callout callout--important">
    <strong>Limited Use.</strong>
    <p>Ferni's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements.</p>
  </div>

  <p>You choose whether to connect your Google account. Each connection asks Google for only what that feature needs, and you can turn it off at any time.</p>

  <h3>What we access, and why</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google Calendar</strong> (not available to connect yet; once it is, only if you connect it): we read and update your calendar events so Ferni can tell you what's coming up, schedule things you ask for, and remind you.</li>
    <li><strong>Gmail, "send email as me"</strong> (only if you turn it on): permission to send email from your Gmail address. Ferni uses it only to send an email you asked Ferni to send, from your own address. This permission cannot read your inbox, and we do not read it. We also receive your email address, so we can show you which account mail goes out from.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>How we use it</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Only to provide or improve the features you can see and turned on.</li>
    <li>Never for advertising, never sold, and never used to build user profiles for anyone else.</li>
    <li>Never used to train or improve AI models, including our own and any third party's.</li>
    <li>No person at Ferni reads it, except when you ask us to (for example, for support), when it's needed for security (for example, investigating abuse), or to comply with the law.</li>
    <li>We transfer it only as needed to provide those features (for example, to the AI model that answers you during a conversation), to comply with the law, or as part of a merger or acquisition with notice to you.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Storage, retention and deletion</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>The access tokens Google gives us are stored encrypted. We keep them until you disconnect the feature or delete your account.</li>
    <li>For an email Ferni sends from your Gmail, our service logs record that an email was sent and Gmail's message ID, never its content.</li>
    <li>Turning off "send email as me" deletes our copy of that permission. Deleting your Ferni account also asks Google to revoke it.</li>
    <li>You can remove Ferni's access to your Google account at any time at <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

